        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "52ff60de-c3ee-50f0-9a8a-20838ef8e66e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Paride ed Elena; Orfeo ed Euridice\n- People: Christoph Willibald Gluck; Ranieri de' Calzabigi; Maria Theresa\n- Places: Vienna; Burgtheater\n- Concepts: Gluck's reform operas; Orpheus myth\n\nFacts:\n- Orfeo ed Euridice is an opera by Christoph Willibald Gluck based on the myth of Orpheus, with a libretto by Ranieri de' Calzabigi.\n- Orfeo ed Euridice was first performed at the Burgtheater in Vienna on 5 October 1762 in the presence of Empress Maria Theresa.\n- Paride ed Elena is the third of Gluck's so-called reform operas for Vienna, following Alceste and Orfeo ed Euridice.\n- Paride ed Elena is the least often performed of those three reform operas.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
